   "title": "How to use",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "TRANSPARENT STICKER\n\n1. Write your subject in the middle of the prompt. Keep the first sentence (This is an RGBA image with transparency.) and the last one (The image has alpha channel and the background is transparent.).\n2. Press Run.\n\nThe PNG keeps real transparency: drop it on any background. Saving as JPG would show a flat purple where it is transparent.\n\n6 GB settings (tested on a 6 GB graphics card with 16 GB of RAM): int8 model and text encoder, the 8-step speed LoRA (8 steps, CFG 1, deis_2m: needs the RES4LYF nodes; or pick euler), comfy kitchen attention, pictures scaled to 1 MP. First run of the day is slower while the files load.\nLicence: Qwen Image 2.1 is under the Qwen Research License (non-commercial)."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "TRANSPARENT STICKER\n\n1. Write your subject in the middle of the prompt. Keep the first sentence (This is an RGBA image with transparency.) and the last one (The image has alpha channel and the background is transparent.).\n2. Press Run.\n\nThe PNG keeps real transparency: drop it on any background. Saving as JPG would show a flat purple where it is transparent.\n\n6 GB settings (tested on a 6 GB graphics card with 16 GB of RAM): int8 model and text encoder, the 8-step speed LoRA (8 steps, CFG 1, deis_2m: needs the RES4LYF nodes; or pick euler), comfy kitchen attention, pictures scaled to 1 MP. First run of the day is slower while the files load.\nLicence: Qwen Image 2.1 is under the Qwen Research License (non-commercial)."
